    <\associate|figure>
      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|7.1>||The
      forward\Ubackward structure of <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:fbsde-system>)>
      on <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<bbb-T\><rsup|2>>, heat profile, at
      resolutions <with|mode|<quote|math>|t<rsub|1>\<less\>t<rsub|2>\<less\>t<rsub|3>\<less\>T>,
      all built from the same noise. Top: the field gains the fluctuation of
      each shell, <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t><rsup|1/2>\<mathd\>W<rsub|t>>,
      and reveals finer modes. Read backward, the same process solves the
      linear equation <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:reversal>)>:
      a Gaussian blurring of <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Phi\><rsub|T>\<sim\>\<nu\><rsub|T>>,
      which does not see the interaction (dashed arrow). Vertical arrows: at
      each resolution the force is the function
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|-\<mathD\>V<rsub|t>> of the field. Bottom: the
      effective force <with|mode|<quote|math>|F<rsub|t>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|t>*<around|[|-\<mathD\>V<rsub|T><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|T>|)>|]>>
      for the <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Phi\><rsup|4>> interaction,
      determined backward from the terminal interaction. It is shown to first
      order in <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<lambda\>>, where it is the Wick cube
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|-<frac|\<lambda\>|3>*H<rsub|3>*<around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|t>;c<rsub|t>|)>>,
      and each panel is in its own units.>|<pageref|auto-10>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|7.2>||A
      zero-dimensional Polchinski process (Exercise
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|ex:zero-dim>):
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|Q<rsub|t>=1-\<mathe\><rsup|-t>>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|T=5>, <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|T><around|(|x|)>=<frac|1|2>*x<rsup|4>-<frac|3|2>*x<rsup|2>>.
      Left: the effective force <with|mode|<quote|math>|F<rsub|t>=-V<rsub|t><rprime|'>>
      is almost linear at low resolution and develops the double-well
      structure as <with|mode|<quote|math>|t\<to\>T>. Centre: paths of the
      FBSDE <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:fbsde>)>,
      which split between the two wells (stochastic localisation). Right:
      histogram of <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Phi\><rsub|T>>
      (<with|mode|<quote|math>|2\<cdot\>10<rsup|4>> paths) against the
      density of <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<nu\><rsub|T>>.>|<pageref|auto-25>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|8.1>||The Polchinski
      equation <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:polchinski>)>
      and the Burgers equation <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:burgers>)>
      as graphs. A blob with <with|mode|<quote|math>|n> legs is the
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|n>-th derivative of
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|t>>, or of the force
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|F<rsub|t>>, whose root is the arrow; a line
      with a dot is the kernel <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>>.
      The first term joins two blobs and makes a tree; the second closes a
      loop on one blob. Integrating from <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|T>>
      and iterating generates the connected Feynman graphs, with lines
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|Q<rsub|T,t>>.>|<pageref|auto-29>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|8.2>||Stochastic
      localisation for a two-component field:
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|Q<rsub|t>=<around|(|1-\<mathe\><rsup|-t>|)>*<with|math-font|<quote|Bbb>|1>>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|T=4>, <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|T>> a
      tilted double well, and the contours show the density of
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<nu\><rsub|T>>. One path of
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:fbsde>)>
      up to resolution <with|mode|<quote|math>|t> (navy), with its terminal
      value <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Phi\><rsub|T>> (open circle). The
      forecast <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<psi\><rsub|t>=\<Phi\><rsub|t>+S<rsub|t>*F<rsub|t>>
      (gold) is the mean of the conditional law
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<Phi\><rsub|t>>>: teal
      samples, and the ellipse is two standard deviations of
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|rm>|font-shape|<quote|right>|Cov>><rsub|t>>.
      At low resolution the conditional law covers both wells; as
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|t> grows it localises on one of
      them.>|<pageref|auto-35>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|8.3>||The
      zero-dimensional model of Figure <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|fig:polchinski-0d>
      at <with|mode|<quote|math>|t=1.2>. Left: the shear
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Sigma\><rsub|t>> (teal arrows) maps the graph
      of the force <with|mode|<quote|math>|F<rsub|t>=-V<rsub|t><rprime|'>>
      (navy) to a graph over the forecast <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<psi\>>
      (gold), which is the graph of <with|mode|<quote|math>|-\<Gamma\><rsub|t><rprime|'>>.
      Right: the bare potential <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|T>>, the
      effective potential <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|t>> and
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Gamma\><rsub|t>>, each shifted to have
      minimum <with|mode|<quote|math>|0>.>|<pageref|auto-41>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|8.4>||The Wetterich
      equation <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:wetterich>)>
      as graphs. The double line is the full response
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<around|(|\<mathD\><rsup|2>\<Gamma\><rsup|<with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|rm>|font-shape|<quote|right>|EAA>>><rsub|t>+\<cal-R\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|-1>=<around|(|S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>+\<mathD\><rsup|2>\<Gamma\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|-1>>
      and the crossed circle is one insertion of
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|t>>. There is
      exactly one loop: the tree term of Figure
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|fig:polchinski-graphs>
      has been absorbed by the Legendre transform. Each field derivative
      brings down a higher vertex, so the hierarchy does not close at a
      finite order. The bottom row expands the response around
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|S<rsub|t>>.>|<pageref|auto-43>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|8.5>||The regulator
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<cal-R\><rsub|t>> of the heat profile
      (<with|mode|<quote|math>|T=\<infty\>>, <with|mode|<quote|math>|m=1>):
      close to the mass term <with|mode|<quote|math>|t<rsup|2>> (dotted) on
      the modes <with|mode|<quote|math>|<around|\||k|\|>\<ll\>t>,
      exponentially small on the modes <with|mode|<quote|math>|<around|\||k|\|>\<gg\>t>.>|<pageref|auto-45>>
    </associate>
